Of course, it depends on the simulation. But from the performance point of view, it is always better to define multiple trajectories and multiple generators. You can create them in a very easy way, with very few lines of code, using lapply, and the performance gains are huge (see this example <http://r-simmer.org/articles/G-ctmc.html#example-2>).

